   "source": [
    "# Target: conversion rate\n",
    "conv_counts = df_raw[\"conversion_flag\"].value_counts().sort_index()\n",
    "conv_pct = df_raw[\"conversion_flag\"].value_counts(normalize=True).sort_index() * 100\n",
    "print(\"Counts:\\n\", conv_counts)\n",
    "print(\"\\nPercentages:\\n\", conv_pct.round(2))\n",
    "print(f\"\\nOverall conversion rate: {df_raw['conversion_flag'].mean():.2%}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Naive rule: predict \"no conversion\" for every customer\n",
    "naive_accuracy = (df_raw[\"conversion_flag\"] == 0).mean()\n",
    "print(f\"\\nNaive accuracy (predict nobody converts): {naive_accuracy:.2%}\")\n",
    "print(\"Converters missed by the naive rule:\", (df_raw[\"conversion_flag\"] == 1).sum(), \"(100%)\")\n",
    "\n",
    "ax = conv_pct.plot(kind=\"bar\")\n",
    "ax.set_title(\"Conversion distribution\")\n",
    "ax.set_xlabel(\"conversion_flag (0 = No, 1 = Yes)\")\n",
    "ax.set_ylabel(\"Customers (%)\")\n",
    "plt.xticks(rotation=0)\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "fc6119f6",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Target.** Only **5.28%** (164 of 3,104) convert; conversion is the clear minority. \"Predict that nobody converts\" gives **94.72% accuracy** while reaching **0 converters**. Accuracy is therefore not a useful success measure. Because the decision is \"who gets one of the limited contacts\", we evaluate **precision among the contacted 12%** (and recall: which share of all converters we reach). Random selection is expected to give ≈5.3% precision — the minimum to beat."
   ]
  },
