   "source": [
    "# Leakage check: columns that are measured AFTER the campaign\n",
    "print(\"Revenue after campaign > 0 vs conversion_flag:\")\n",
    "print(pd.crosstab(df_raw[\"conversion_flag\"], df_raw[\"purchase_revenue_after_campaign_eur\"] > 0))\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\nClicks after campaign by conversion (mean / median):\")\n",
    "print(df_raw.groupby(\"conversion_flag\")[\"clicks_after_campaign\"].agg([\"mean\", \"median\"]).round(2))\n",
    "\n",
    "data = df_raw[[\"previous_orders_12m\", \"days_since_last_order\", \"avg_basket_eur_12m\",\n",
    "               \"campaign_cost_eur\", \"clicks_after_campaign\", \"purchase_revenue_after_campaign_eur\", \"conversion_flag\"]]\n",
    "matrix = data.corr()\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(9, 6))\n",
    "sns.heatmap(matrix, annot=True, fmt=\".2f\", cmap=\"YlOrRd\", linewidths=0.5, linecolor=\"white\")\n",
    "plt.title(\"Correlation matrix (incl. post-campaign columns)\")\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "4f4b339d",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Leakage.** `purchase_revenue_after_campaign_eur` is > 0 **exactly** when `conversion_flag` = 1 (2,940/0 and 0/164): it *is* the target in another form. Converters also click far more after the campaign (median 2 vs 0 clicks). Both are only known **after** the campaign, so they cannot be used at the prediction moment → excluded in **D5**. The correlation matrix confirms that, apart from these two leakage columns, the pre-campaign variables only have weak correlations with conversion; `days_since_last_order` is the strongest (negative)."
   ]
  },
