    "**D3 – Discount units.** *Evidence:* the same offers are stored as fraction (0.15) and as percent (15). *Technique:* values < 1 × 100. *Verification:* the crosstab shows a one-to-one mapping into 4 levels (0/5/10/15%). *Interpretation:* conversion by discount is 4.7% / 5.7% / 4.5% / 6.0% — **no steady increase with a higher discount**. For the business: the data does not show that bigger discounts buy more conversions. *Next decision:* keep `discount_pct` as a feature (it is known before sending), but do not use the model to recommend discount levels."
