   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "de99619d",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Encoding and scaling.** `get_dummies(drop_first=True)` turns tier and channel into 4 dummies; `MinMaxScaler` puts all features on 0–1 so the logistic regression coefficients can be compared. Scaling uses only feature values, never the target, so it does not leak conversion information. **Validation strategy:** there is no date in the data, so a time-based split is impossible (limitation). We use **5-fold cross-validation (`cross_val_predict`, cv=5)**: every customer is predicted by a model that did not see that customer, and with `cv=5` scikit-learn keeps the ~5% conversion rate in every fold."
   ]
