   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "544b18ce",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Errors in business terms (per 1,000 customers, 120 contacts)**\n",
    "- **False positives (wasted contacts):** ≈109 of 120 contacted customers do not buy, even with the model. At €1.39 per contact the money risk is small; the bigger risk is annoying customers (opt-outs).\n",
    "- **False negatives (missed converters):** ≈41 of ≈53 converters are not contacted, because capacity is 12% and the signal is weak.\n",
    "- **Value:** at the same contact cost (€167), gross revenue from contacted customers rises from ≈€567 (random) to ≈€857 (recency) and ≈€1,000 (model). The model needs a **16.7% margin to break even — but only if every purchase was caused by the campaign.** Recent loyal buyers may have bought anyway, so the real extra value is unknown and probably lower."
   ]
  },
