   "source": [
    "### Decision: **PILOT** the logistic regression — not full deployment\n",
    "\n",
    "**Why not \"do not deploy\":** criteria 1–3 are met. The model doubles the hit rate of random targeting (9.5% vs 5.3%), beats the simple recency rule (35 vs 30 converters) and does so in all three campaigns.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Why not full deployment:**\n",
    "1. The gain over the recency rule is **5 converters on 370 contacts** — real in direction, but small; it must be confirmed on a new campaign.\n",
    "2. The business goal is *extra* sales. Every customer in the data was contacted, so we **cannot measure uplift**. The model mostly selects recent Gold buyers, who may buy anyway.\n",
    "3. The model never contacts customers inactive for 180+ days.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Limitations:** weak signal; no dates (no time-based validation); 18 records with 0 orders but a basket value; margin unknown; small numbers of converters per segment; the 12% capacity is an assumption.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Return to earlier phase:** after the pilot, go back to **Phase 1** (define the goal as *extra* sales) and **Phase 2** (data with a control group)."
   ]
